    },
    "body": "Adds sandboxing options that `bitcoind` doesn't need to be exempt from, namely kernel/clock/hostname protection, namespace, realtime and SUID restrictions, a socket address family allowlist, and a system call filter and empty capability bounding set.\n\nAlso switches the `ExecStartPre` `chgrp` from \"!\" to \"+\", since \"!\" only lifts `User=`/`Group=`, and the new syscall filter and capability bounding set would block it otherwise.",
    "labels": [],
